# Paste the firebaseConfig object from the Firebase console here, as JSON, on
# one line. These values are not secrets — every Firebase web app ships them to
# the browser. What keeps your calendar private is the security rules.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill it in. Leave it out and the app runs
# without sync, saving to the browser as before.
VITE_FIREBASE_CONFIG={"apiKey":"…","authDomain":"…firebaseapp.com","projectId":"…","storageBucket":"….firebasestorage.app","messagingSenderId":"…","appId":"…"}
